From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dsi/phy: initialize PLL bias when enabling the PHY

PHY enable establishes a PLL bias reference and sets the power bits, but
leaves PLL_SYSTEM_MUXES uninitialized. Subsequent bias gets skip the
register writes because the reference is already held, including the
slave bias get during bonded PLL prepare.

Initialize PLL_SYSTEM_MUXES while establishing the PHY reference and allow
the bias to settle before continuing. The existing reference stays held
across host power on, so temporary clock operations cannot power down the
PLL and lose its register contents.

Fixes: cb55f39bf7b1 ("drm/msm/dsi/phy: Fix reading zero as PLL rates when unprepared")
Link: https://git.kernel.org/torvalds/c/cb55f39bf7b1e687b88dc9825c21a7d3454b5acb
Link: https://www.mail-archive.com/dri-devel@lists.freedesktop.org/msg638716.html

WHY WE NEED IT.  Pocket S2 is the only board we ship in DSI BONDED mode --
`qcom,dual-dsi-mode` + `qcom,sync-dual-dsi` in sm8650-ayaneo-ps2.dts, one
1440x2560 panel driven across two DSI links.  Linux 7.2.6 reverted
93c97bc8d85d ("drm/msm: dsi: fix PLL init in bonded mode") as 5de981b7db1f
(upstream 44784327815b), and with that revert only the BOTTOM HALF of the
panel draws: HW-observed on 7.2.6, 2026-09-14.  The slave PHY never gets
its mux written, because dsi_7nm_phy_enable() pre-sets pll_enable_cnt = 1
and every later dsi_pll_enable_pll_bias() early-returns.

WHY NOT RE-APPLY 93c97bc8d85d.  This slot used to carry that revert of the
revert.  It fixes bonded mode by turning the bias into a plain refcount,
but then a transient bias get/put (vco_recalc_rate, pll_save_state) can
drop the count to zero, and dsi_pll_disable_pll_bias() clears
PLL_SHUTDOWNB and the mux.  Without PLL_SHUTDOWNB most PLL registers read
as zero, so CCF gets a zero divisor and non-bonded panels come up in the
wrong mode -- the regression upstream reverted it for.  This patch keeps
the reference phy_enable holds and only adds the one write it was missing.

DROP THIS PATCH once Neil Armstrong's bonded-mode rework lands in the
pinned stable series -- check whether dsi_7nm_phy_enable() still assigns
pll_enable_cnt = 1 without writing PLL_SYSTEM_MUXES.  If that has changed,
re-evaluate rather than carry it forward.

---

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c
@@ -1096,7 +1096,9 @@
 	data = DSI_7nm_PHY_CMN_CTRL_0_DIGTOP_PWRDN_B |
 	       DSI_7nm_PHY_CMN_CTRL_0_PLL_SHUTDOWNB;
 	writel(data, base + REG_DSI_7nm_PHY_CMN_CTRL_0);
+	writel(0xc0, phy->pll_base + REG_DSI_7nm_PHY_PLL_SYSTEM_MUXES);
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&pll->pll_enable_lock, flags);
+	ndelay(250);
 
 	/* Assert PLL core reset */
 	writel(0x00, base + REG_DSI_7nm_PHY_CMN_PLL_CNTRL);
